A||N||5||84redfiero||Help!!! engine won't start.||||1||
Z||000000||84redfiero||11-19-2000||09:55 PM||||just put my engine in after replacing the clutch and now it won't start it will turn over but it sounds like no fuel is getting into the engine  i replaced the fuel filter and tbi the engine is a 2.5 liter four-cylinder 4 speed  please send me any ideas or information you have it would be helpfull thank you<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||11-19-2000||10:07 PM||||hey that's the same way i started the forum was with a "help" problem.  well i have no idea about your car, sorry.  but newayz...welcome to the club  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||10
Z||000002||JohnnyK||11-19-2000||11:11 PM||||I don't know if this would do it, but maybe that could happen if you put the fuel filter in backwards? Also, are you sure it's fuel and not spark? I just did mine to and had problems, but then realized I had the ignition firing all wrong. But to make sure, take off your air cleaner and watch the TBI and have someone crank it over. It should spray.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-20-2000||01:53 AM||||Check the connector for the oil pressure. This also can cause the fuel pump to not work.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||11-20-2000||11:38 AM||||I mention this only because it happened to me.  Have you done a careful check to make sure all the wiring harness connectors are plugged in?  There is a single connector that kind of hides behind the heat shield on the firewall above the catalytic converter.  It is the power lead for the fuel pump and if it's not COMPLETELY plugged in the pump won't work.  Don't ask how I know this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||11-20-2000||12:32 PM||||Hmmm.. If you find you're getting gas at the TBI, look to see if your getting a stray spark between the coil wire/terminal to the coil bracket.  It happened to me after a complete engine harness swap.  Just cleaned the terminal with some sandpaper and it fired right up.  <P>BTW<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerwelcome.gif"> ||||reg||1
